In the dualpi2_change() function, the limit enforcement loop (lines 469-477) calls qdisc_dequeue_internal(sch, true) and immediately dereferences the returned skb pointer (e.g., skb->truesize) without checking if it is NULL: 

	while (qdisc_qlen(sch) > sch->limit ||
	       q->memory_used > q->memory_limit) {
		struct sk_buff *skb = qdisc_dequeue_internal(sch, true);

		q->memory_used -= skb->truesize;
		qdisc_qstats_backlog_dec(sch, skb);
		rtnl_qdisc_drop(skb, sch);
	}

If the dequeue operation returns NULL (for instance, if the C-queue is empty but packets remain in the L-queue, or due to other internal state), this results in a NULL pointer dereference.
